{#
================================================================================
[NOTES]
================================================================================
Prompt: polish_chapter.j2
Service Step: POLISH_CHAPTER (Chapter Polishing)
Purpose: Perform final polish on the chapter to bring it to publishing-quality literary standards.
Upstream Inputs:
  - chapter_text: Chapter body text from EditStep output
  - stage_cards.source: ChapterSourceSlice, containing source boundary and style/voice projection (if provided by caller)
  - eval_summary: Evaluation summary from EvaluateStep
  - repair_hints: Evaluation suggestions from EvaluateStep
  - continuity_notes: Continuity issues from ContinuityEval / ContinuityRepair
  - style_profile: From StyleProfile
Downstream Outputs:
  - text: Polished chapter body as plain text
  - Downstream consumers: CheckChapterStep / PersistStep
Consumption Chain Priority:
  P0 = immutable_facts / POV rules / word count ±10% constraint
  P1 = continuity_notes (continuity repair) / repair_hints (evaluation suggestions)
  P2 = literary style / sensory variety / dialogue density
Brief Example:
  Input: chapter_text="Lin Yuan stood at the city gate...", eval_summary="Pacing is somewhat slow"
  Output: "In the morning mist, Lin Yuan's figure appeared at the city gate..." (plain text)
================================================================================
#}

